        {
          "path": "_m/9/q/8/y/sutro-tower-wk/fog-shadow-tv-tower.jpg",
          "filename": "Fog shadow tv tower.jpg",
          "caption": "Fog shadow of Sutro tower, San Francisco.\n\nThese fascinating shadows look odd since humans are not used to seeing shadows in three dimensions. The thin fog was just dense enough to be illuminated by the light that passed through the gaps in a structure or in a tree. As a result, the path of an object shadow through the \"fog\" appears darkened. In a sense, these shadow lanes are similar to crepuscular rays, which are caused by cloud shadows, but here, they're caused by an object shadows.(The description was provided by Dr. Andy Young.)",
          "alt": "Fog shadow of Sutro tower, San Francisco.\n\nThese fascinating shadows look odd since humans are not used to seeing shadows in three dimensions. The thin fog was just dense enough to be illuminated by the light that passed through the gaps in a structure or in a tree. As a result, the path of an object shadow through the \"fog\" appears darkened. In a sense, these shadow lanes are similar to crepuscular rays, which are caused by cloud shadows, but here, they're caused by an object shadows.(The description was provided by Dr. Andy Young.)",
          "width": 779,
          "height": 1000,
